 - **One title everywhere:** a tab label, a link card's title and the page's own h1 all read the sub-page's own `title` (the last `title` in its `page.jsonl`, else its `page.js`; `LivePage.title_of`). To rename a sub-page, set its title on its own path: `item({path: "/live/demos/", delta: {"title": "Feature demos"}})`. A link card's `title` shows only until the page's own one arrives.
 - **The breadcrumb is the url** (`location.pathname`, word for word, every step a link): a phone hides the address bar, so this is where the owner reads it. It redraws on every url change, a tab switch included (`LivePage.on_url`), and the tab row lights the tab the url is in.
 - **Settings** (the gear, `<page>/settings/`): first the class file that draws the page (`LivePage.js`, or `DesignPage.js` on /live/design/), a tap opens its code; then, for a card or a saved screen, which `page.jsonl` it is saved in; then the page's folder, labelled with its path ("/live"), one list top to bottom: folders, then files, `page.jsonl` included (`LivePage.Files`). A folder opens its own list (`/live/settings/doc/`); a file opens its code on its own page, the full width with no line numbers, highlighted by ext/highlight (`/live/settings/LivePage.js/`), and the header's small **raw** link is the file itself. Every settings page is a LivePage with its own gear: `/live/settings/LivePage.js/settings/` is that page's settings. A folder or a saved screen named `settings` wins over it.
